 2026-10-07  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

   * release 0.10: the first release since 0.9. ChangeLog entries stopped in
     2005; since then the work is recorded in fixes/ (one numbered patch per
     fixed bug, 1-400) and the git log. Highlights of this release:
     - 6151 of the cases in yash's POSIX suite pass, 7 fail (two of them on
       purpose, as echo and cat are builtins); 6103 more need a terminal
     - break/continue in a sourced file, set -o ignoreeof, set -v for . and
       eval, $LINENO in eval, ls -C/-x, head/tail headers for empty files,
       ulimit -H in a subshell, $(...) output of forked functions
     - SHISH_TRACE: a runtime-selectable trace of the evaluator (debug builds),
       documented in doc/debug-output.md
     - WebAssembly (Emscripten and WASI) builds and a browser playground
     - cpack packages: a tarball and a .deb
     Known gaps: job control under a real terminal, bash's += and <(...), fc,
     vi mode; see BUGS.

 2005-04-30  Roman Senn  <smoli (at) paranoya.ch>

   * there have been no ChangeLog entries for a long time
     while development was in progress. I don't think detailed
     ChangeLog entries are already required at this time, because 
     shish is under heavy development by just one person. However
     I will write ChangeLog entries about major achievments and
     design changes/improvements.

   * the development is currently suspended due to the need of
     a libsgui release (http://www.blah.ch/libsgui/)
     shish development will be resumed in a month or so.
     

